From 553ca63b8fe1d38c0856bc5cc63cff04a4559c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the GPU Landlock policy read /system/lib64

Encrypted video has not played on Android 16 and later. The CDM lives
in the GPU process, and Android's MediaDrm class loads libmedia_jni.so
from /system/lib64 the first time a page uses it. By then the GPU
process has applied Landlock, and /system/lib64 is not on its read-only
list, so the load fails, createMediaKeys() rejects with "Disconnection
error" and Widevine video never starts. The same failed load keeps
MediaCodecList from initialising in that process.

/system/lib64 holds Android's own system libraries, which any app can
already read, so the GPU process now gets read access to that directory
and Landlock stays on. Phones on Android 15 and earlier never apply
Landlock and were not affected.

Upstream's list is unchanged as of M158. Regular Chrome on phones never
turns this sandbox on, so only desktop-class Android builds run into it.
---
 sandbox/policy/linux/landlock_gpu_policy_android.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sandbox/policy/linux/landlock_gpu_policy_android.cc b/sandbox/policy/linux/landlock_gpu_policy_android.cc
index 997a5b7819a..9b2070fde2f 100644
--- a/sandbox/policy/linux/landlock_gpu_policy_android.cc
+++ b/sandbox/policy/linux/landlock_gpu_policy_android.cc
@@ -120,7 +120,11 @@ bool ApplyLandlock(sandbox::mojom::Sandbox sandbox_type) {
       // TODO(crbug.com/462103953): tighten these broad rules once the Corsola
       // issue is resolved and we've confirmed the precise paths needed.
       "/system/vendor/lib", "/system/vendor/lib64", "/vendor/lib",
-      "/vendor/lib64"};
+      "/vendor/lib64",
+      // Android loads libmedia_jni.so from here the first time a page uses
+      // MediaDrm, after this policy is in place. Without it Widevine
+      // video cannot create a CDM.
+      "/system/lib64"};
   uint64_t ro_access =
       LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_READ_FILE | LANDLOCK_ACCESS_FS_READ_DIR;
   if (!AddRulesToPolicy(ruleset_fd.get(), allowed_ro_paths, ro_access)) {
-- 
